{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107226-space-tellurian-vs-technocratic-paradigm","id":1107226,"title":"Space! (tellurian vs technocratic paradigm)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-23T23:11:59-07:00","id":1107226,"title":"Space! (tellurian vs technocratic paradigm)","content":"So hey folks, <br /> Here's something that's been bugging me, I hope you can help. <br /> I've not got very far into the book of worlds yet, but from everything I've read so far, there's no such thing as space, only the umbra, and the technocratic paradigm defines the umbra as space. <br /> Now given the fact that the penumbra is meant to be the first realm one reaches after stepping sideways, how come nasa goes straight from earth to the horizon? <br /> Actually that's just one issue I have, while overall I just have real cognitive dissonance. As a &quot;sleeper physics graduate&quot; in our world, I can think of tons of issues with the idea of space just being the umbra. I'm looking to try and get a grip on how it works in WoD please! <br /> <br /> Is everything space agencies like nasa do fakery to convince the masses and therefore create space? <br /> Does the technocracy police every child with a telescope? <br /> How does Kepler spot exoplanets and look at different stars if everything outside our solar system is the far umbra? <br /> How come sleepers can do so much in the way of astrophysics if it's all meant to be the umbra? <br /> <br /> Waaaaa! Etc. <br /> <br /> Thanks in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T01:56:36-07:00","id":1107263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eyrelliah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107226-space-tellurian-vs-technocratic-paradigm#post1107226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the technocracy police every child with a telescope?</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno how true this is, but consider this:<br /> There is no need to police every telescope if the telescopes themselves (as well as perhaps the theory behind them) are constructed in a way the precludes discoveries which are not in line with the lines of reasoning and thought of, at first the Order of Reason, and later of the Technocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 06-24-2017, 05:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T02:00:39-07:00","id":1107265,"title":"","content":"Ah, the umbra. The single most confounding aspect of the World of Darkness<br /> <br /> The thing to keep in mind is that, in Mage, the Umbra shifts and changes constantly depending on the assumptions of the viewer. You've probably already come across the videre of the penumbra, that's one example. Mages such as Hermetics, Virtual Adepts, and the Akashics will see the Astral Videre, and even then their individual perceptions will be slightly varied, The Akashic might see the spirits of their ancestors, and perhaps a couple of dragons floating about, the Hermetic will see a number of angels, and the Adept may see the numbers that code up the Matrix (it's all paradigm specific).<br /> <br /> Dreamspeakers and some Verbena will have a more consistent experience, seeing the Videre Spiritum and having a similar experience to the Garou when they look through the penumbra. while Euthanatos and certain Hollow Ones will instead see the very surface of the Shadowlands of Wraith.<br /> <br /> This same principle of paradigm based access holds true for the rest of the umbra as well. While the penumbra videre are all in the same location, the rest of the umbra is a bit more dramatically detached.<br /> <br /> If you manage to make it to the middle umbra, also known as the Spirit Wilds, the more technologically minded of us may have a hard time accessing all of it. The Astral Heights, for example, are completely cut off. Any Adept that tries to fly above the clouds of the middle umbra, instead of seeing the great pantheon of spiritual incarna, they will go directly into the cold and dark stratosphere. Space as defined by the Technocrats.<br /> <br /> This is explained a bit more in both the Infinite Tapestry and the revised Void Engineer's book. Suffice to say that the Technocracy never really experience the exact same kind of space as other mages, and the more technomancer type mages are likely to experience a different space themselves.<br /> <br /> Space works exactly how you believe it to work. If the mage thinks it'll be a vacuum up there, then it will be. If they think you can breathe the ether, then they can, if they think they can literally walk through the stars or along the pathways provided by the gods, then they can.<br /> <br /> Humanity sees what they expect to see. If they've lived all their life thinking that space is what the Technocrats think it is, then that's what they see. Children might see things a bit different, but then they've always had rather over-active imaginations<br /> <br /> Things get a bit more complicated the deeper you go, but the long and short of it is that there are many different layers to space, and like the videre, they are all in the same place, yet not quite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 06-24-2017, 12:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T06:33:06-07:00","id":1107293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eyrelliah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107226-space-tellurian-vs-technocratic-paradigm#post1107226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So hey folks,<br /> Here's something that's been bugging me, I hope you can help.<br /> I've not got very far into the book of worlds yet, but from everything I've read so far, there's no such thing as space, only the umbra, and the technocratic paradigm defines the umbra as space.<br /> Now given the fact that the penumbra is meant to be the first realm one reaches after stepping sideways, how come nasa goes straight from earth to the horizon?<br /> Actually that's just one issue I have, while overall I just have real cognitive dissonance. As a &quot;sleeper physics graduate&quot; in our world, I can think of tons of issues with the idea of space just being the umbra. I'm looking to try and get a grip on how it works in WoD please!<br /> <br /> Is everything space agencies like nasa do fakery to convince the masses and therefore create space?<br /> Does the technocracy police every child with a telescope?<br /> How does Kepler spot exoplanets and look at different stars if everything outside our solar system is the far umbra?<br /> How come sleepers can do so much in the way of astrophysics if it's all meant to be the umbra?<br /> <br /> Waaaaa! Etc.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's more on space in the Void Engineers Convention book. In essence space as we modern folk know it is called Conventional Space in Mage. Conventional space is... essentially areas of the Umbra the Technocracy has conquered and forced to follow the laws of physics. Most of what space agencies like NASA do is provide human eyes on the subject, which extends the Anthropic Effect out into the Umbra, which forces the Umbra to follow the rules, which creates Conventional Space which is then Seperate from Umbral 'subspace'<br /> <br /> In previous editions, Conventional Space was HUGE, extending over a large chunk of the galaxy. But as of revised and the Dimensional Anomaly/Avatar Storm most of that space was just... lost. Chewed back up by the Umbra.f<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T11:15:41-07:00","id":1107374,"title":"","content":"Interesting! Thanks folks. I guess I still find it strange that the umbra is meant to be a reflection of earth at least in the nearby bit. So a tradition mage can step sideways on earth and see their own interpretation of the penumbra, but a void engineer does the same thing and sees what? They're in space? What happens if they encounter umbrood?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T11:52:36-07:00","id":1107391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eyrelliah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107226-space-tellurian-vs-technocratic-paradigm#post1107226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've not got very far into the book of worlds yet, but from everything I've read so far, there's no such thing as space, only the umbra, and the technocratic paradigm defines the umbra as space.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Book of Worlds discusses &quot;consensual space&quot; - the Earth-realm parallel to Umbral space, on our side of the Gauntlet - on page 138. As we are on the Earthrealm side of the Gauntlet, our telescopes show Consensual space, in the same way that we cannot look through a microscope and see spirits, and non-Awakened vessels stay within Consensual Space (and, as Enginseer noted, actually help to expand it by thickening the Gauntlet) for the same reason a plane leaving Earthly Des Moines lands in Earthly Tulsa.<br /> <br /> (You may be getting tripped up by the metaphysical position of the Book of Worlds, which treats the Earth Realm as just one of many options, rather than drawing a stark &quot;Real vs. Umbral&quot; divide.)<br /> <br /> Space has a very thin Gauntlet, to the point of near non-existence in places, and at the periphery of Conventional Space (the Far Horizon), it basically fails altogether. This doesn't mean that Space ceases to exist beyond that point, merely that the barrier that separates that Realm from others becomes fallible. CB:Void Engineers notes that (as per the telescope example above) we just can't perceive all the nonsense happening beyond that point (most of the time.)<br /> <br /> Now, <i>in addition, </i>Technocratic experience of umbral Realms (&quot;subspace&quot;) has generally hewed closer to their expectations of Earthrealm physics. This is why they use rocketships to go to the Far Horizon instead of psychedelic mushrooms, and why in the Near Horizon they have historically required protective equipment - their experience of that Realm of subspace is that its physical conditions were akin, but not identical, to the physical conditions of the parallel Earthrealm space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T11:59:18-07:00","id":1107393,"title":"","content":"I like that consensual space is screwed since the avatar storm. <br /> Is there any update on any of this in m20?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T12:01:14-07:00","id":1107394,"title":"","content":"Also thanks five eyes - nicely put!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T09:21:36-07:00","id":1107657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eyrelliah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107226-space-tellurian-vs-technocratic-paradigm?p=1107393#post1107393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like that consensual space is screwed since the avatar storm.<br /> Is there any update on any of this in m20?</div> </div> </div> </div>Either it wasn't that big of deal, never happened or got better. The default assumption for M20 is that it &quot;got better&quot;. The others are dealt with via &quot;Purple Box&quot; alternatives. <br /> <br /> If you want to have a VE Chronicle a la the VE book, the default assumption works best for the most part. There are a few issues relating to the Avatar Storm but they don't prohibit VE's with enough oomph from getting into Conventional Space (maybe sort of a penalty for screwing up the Proceedure...) And/or just build your Voidship to handle it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T09:32:12-07:00","id":1107660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eyrelliah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107226-space-tellurian-vs-technocratic-paradigm?p=1107374#post1107374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting! Thanks folks. I guess I still find it strange that the umbra is meant to be a reflection of earth at least in the nearby bit. So a tradition mage can step sideways on earth and see their own interpretation of the penumbra, but a void engineer does the same thing and sees what? They're in space? What happens if they encounter umbrood?</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends....<br /> <br /> This is all part of the mass confusion that is Mage. Which is glorious, subject to POV issues, has to be hashed out how you want to handle it in your own game, is full of massive internal contradictions that are typically only made worse by each attempt to codify an &quot;orthodoxy&quot;.<br /> <br /> Perhaps when VE's or other users of Dimensional Science use their abilities on Earth, they access what they are looking for. The VE's and NWO Ghosbusters don't access &quot;outer space&quot; when they do their thing, they look into the Underworld. Some VE's are still exploring the uncharted regions of the planet. If they were to use Dimensional Science they would probably access &quot;alternate Earths&quot; in a sort of string-theory-esque or even just find something that needs to be mapped and understood and made mundane enough to put on a map like the Void Engineers were doing while they were going all imperialistic and colonial during the Age of Exploration and mapped a lot of the wonder out of the world back in the Order of Reason days. <br /> <br /> And then there are the largest part of the VE's whose mission really seems to be trying to get the Masses to buy into their particular Umbral Realm of choice (which is both something they chose but also something that is being affected by their expectations, those of the Masses and, in a feedback loop, what they discover is modifying what they think they will find). Probably a part of the whole mission has to do with getting everyone to believe in Conventional Space as the way in which the vastness of the Umbra works to make the rest of the Umbra more and more difficult to access from both sides. Notice that the Conventional Space they are pushing, particularly in the Solar System is very low on EDE's, Venus-as-Hell, Mars as barren waste with any chance of life being long gone... Hells, Europa is probably being set up for another &quot;See! We told you there is no life anywhere but Earth!&quot; to further the agenda. (Which doesn't mean that there might not be EDE's on Europa, but they will be killed off with prejudice and the Masses won't know a thing about them, ever.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T07:24:51-07:00","id":1108019,"title":"","content":"I've evolved my own interpretation to replace the one in the books.<br /> <br /> Back when the Order of Reason first got going, the proto-VE was divided into two groups - the Celestial Masters and the Void Seekers. The Void Seekers traveled the mundane world, discovering new lands and peoples, and claiming them in the name of wherever they came from. The Celestial Masters explored the Umbra instead - first by sailing ships &quot;straight&quot; rather than following the curve of the Earth, and therefore up into the sky, and later by flying airships directly upwards. So - their method for Umbral travel was simply &quot;go up high enough&quot;.<br /> <br /> Originally, the Celestial Masters thought they'd reach some lovely Heavens or whatnot. Of course, they didn't - they found all sorts of Umbral nastiness, like creatures alien to their experience, and started to doubt their mission. But eventually they keep going, now with lots more weapons on their skyships. So - you don't just find the Umbra you seek, you find the Umbra that is there; otherwise they would have actually reached the Heavens they sought. But you can travel to the Umbra by whatever method works for you.<br /> <br /> Reformed later as the Void Engineers, they discarded the ether/phlogiston theories of the Sons of Ether and instead decided that beyond the Horizon (that is, beyond the atmosphere) was a dead vacuum of space. So they set out to make it so. They went on expeditions in their voidships and formatted whatever was in that Umbral realm before into dead, empty Conventional Space. Then conventional human space exploration went into those formatted zones to reinforce the Consensus belief in that - and they use the Consensual method of getting there (going up high enough). So the VEs go out further all the time, formatting Umbra into Conventional Space like you would an old hard drive. As they do so, they encounter Tradition mages whose realms are built to accommodate them without all the space suits and nonsense that the VEs come dressed up with - a Dreamspeaker around a fire, for example - and they fix that right up so that being without a spacesuit there is deadly. They also encounter loads of Umbrood that they dispatch with plasma rifles and such. It's sort of like Making Space Safe for No One, a scorched-earth approach. They see the farther parts of the Umbra only as sources of danger. As they go, they set up Constructs as military outposts or things to trade to other Conventions to get more plasma rifles.<br /> <br /> There are of course other areas of the Umbra. The Near Umbra, not beyond the Horizon, is more contested and the VEs don't currently plan to make it quite so homogenous as Conventional Space; completely deadening it tends to have deleterious effects on the actual world of which it is a reflection. The Low Umbra creeps most VEs out and they typically avoid it (especially if you include the Avatar Storm and its sparking events). And naturally they aren't done with the Deep Umbra yet, and they lose ground to Nephandi monstrosities, Marauders, or Ethership armadas just as often as they gain it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7356,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","user":"haldir2012","date":". 06-26-2017, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T09:58:44-07:00","id":1108053,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7356\" data-vbnamecard=\"7356\">haldir2012</a> SO, the Horizon/Etherspace doesn't exist in your Mage? The place where the most emblematic Traditional mage fortresses are it's a vacuum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-26-2017, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T11:55:01-07:00","id":1108089,"title":"","content":"Not entirely - but the VE are trying to make it that way. <br /> <br /> It weirds me out that places like Mars are both beyond the Horizon (and thus in theory Umbral in nature) but also have a Penumbra of their own. So I simplify it by saying that everything beyond the atmosphere/Horizon is Umbral, but that the VE are trying to format it all into an empty vacuum while also reinforcing the Consensus that you enter this Umbra by flying upwards. So as it becomes Conventional Space, it is less and less like Umbra; it doesn't do interesting things, you don't reach it by stepping sideways, etc. - to the point that non-Enlightened personnel can ride on the space shuttle and get there on their own. They aren't yet done, so the unformatted regions get blocked from humanity's view (e.g., Doissetep is filtered from all high-res telescope images of Mars, several Constructs stand like watchtowers along the border between formatted Conventional Space and unformatted Etherspace).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T07:03:59-07:00","id":1108383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It weirds me out that places like Mars are both beyond the Horizon (and thus in theory Umbral in nature) but also have a Penumbra of their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is that Mars ISN'T beyond the Horizon, as per the Book of Worlds (and every other) it's <i>inside </i>the Horizon (Horizon starts in the upper atmosphere and ends in the Asteroid Belt in Revised, and outside the solar system before that, so, technically it would be arround that area). This is why Doissetep it's a Horizon Realm<br /> <br /> It's my understanding that here Umbras overlap like an onion. You have Conventional Mars on one layer (what mundane astronomers see. VE book say you can get here with Forces), Horizon/Etherspace on the other layer (what Mages see, VE say that to get here you need DimSci), The Aetherial Realm (seen by werebeasts, Dreamspeakers, and some primordial mages, VE can't get here as per the Book of Worlds) and there may even be a &quot;Deep Umbra&quot; layer somewhere over there ('cus Shard Realms are supposed to be in the Deep, but that isn't very clear). All these spaces are very distinct, in the VE Convention Book it's stated that their ships can shift between Conventional Space and Horizon(what they call &quot;Subspace&quot;), and they need different Sphere combinations to travel to these places<br /> <br /> Mars, like our own planet, has a Penumbra...meaning that you go from Horizon/Aetherial to the Penumbra just like you were entering in the Earth's Middle Umbra from there...but this isn't necessary, you can shift directly from Etherspace to Conventional without entering &quot;Martian Middle Umbra&quot; because these spaces aren't one above the other (like Middle/Aetherial), but rather layers (like Middle/Dark/Astral). You can get from one to the other, the mistery of why astronomers don't see Doissetep it's answered the same way as why they don't see ghosts. The same way, astronauts can get to outer space in Earth without needing to shift to the Umbra (if you go to Conventional Space, if you go to Horizon you need to enter any of the three Umbras and go up, or just step sideways in outer space)<br /> <br /> The problem with this it's the insistence of VE that there's no Conventional Space outside the Asteroid Belt. They say that astronomers are being fooled by an ilusion effect that the outer Horizon has...I think this it's bullshit, but it's necessary so that VE can keep their hipe of being resposible of the void in outer space. I would much rather have the entire universe being covered in Material Outer Space, with the Deep being just another layer","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-27-2017, 10:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T14:44:43-07:00","id":1108949,"title":"","content":"Well thanks folks, I feel like I've failed a seeking... <br /> <br /> Can't get it in my head still BUT the confused mess is much, much richer now. I will cherry-pick if my players ever go to space!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T09:35:38-07:00","id":1109283,"title":"","content":"Mage is all about cherry picking. Hell, roleplaying games are all about cherry picking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13562-lordmagnusen","name":"lordmagnusen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T09:57:14-07:00","id":1109293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lordmagnusen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107226-space-tellurian-vs-technocratic-paradigm?p=1109283#post1109283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage is all about cherry picking. Hell, roleplaying games are all about cherry picking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. I ran a Son of Ether in Space game for awhile and I tossed as much as I kept. I used whatever worked to tell the stories I wanted to tell and the players wanted to play and chucked the rest. For example, having the Asteroid Belt as the &quot;Horizon&quot; and the outer Solar System as Deep Umbra just didn't work for us at all. Racing around the moons of Jupiter was a major part of the game and applying the rules from <i>here </i>or the ones from <i>there </i>(probably not both, since they are mutually exclusive) about how things work in the Deep Umbra, how to get there, etc.would have been a drag on the game. So POOF! The Horizon moves out to the heliopause. That's not in any book, but it worked for us and, to me, makes more sense than RAW. <br /> <br /> Hells, in empty space, the boundaries were pretty much non-existent between the Conventional Space of the Void Engineers, whatever it was that those Nephandi &quot;screamships&quot; were traveling through and the &quot;outer space&quot; through which the PCs were in (which was NOT Etherspace as described, it was more a version of outer space between a Ray Bradbury Mars, a Venus of steamy jungles and a Moon with the ruins of a lost civilization). So we COULD have space battles between ships from all three different groups without having dimensional boundaries getting in the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 06-29-2017, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T08:16:45-07:00","id":1109767,"title":"","content":"That's the way (uh-huh uh-huh) I like it, Ajax. You made me miss my old Mages in Space game, we were a mostly Etherite, but with some other trads (like a Ghost Wheel Society Dreamspeaker), and I was the ship's Chief Engineer, Professor Zharkov, former Soviet rocket scientist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13562-lordmagnusen","name":"lordmagnusen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T13:32:12-07:00","id":1109905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lordmagnusen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107226-space-tellurian-vs-technocratic-paradigm?p=1109767#post1109767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the way (uh-huh uh-huh) I like it, Ajax. You made me miss my old Mages in Space game, we were a mostly Etherite, but with some other trads (like a Ghost Wheel Society Dreamspeaker), and I was the ship's Chief Engineer, Professor Zharkov, former Soviet rocket scientist.</div> </div> </div> </div>We had one character &quot;go Cultist&quot; during the game (she was the pilot... which meant that getting from place to place got a little weird...) and another fronted the points for Dual Tradition and was a Virtual Adept/Etherite, the communications officer. <br /> <br /> The others were pure Etherite. Well... except for the one whose body was infected with fungus that resisted their scientific efforts to cure. He ended up as a brain in a jar and couldn't really do any science anymore. Eventually, they built a little chassis with spider legs on it for the brain to walk around on it's own. Said character was very upset with the rest of the group and kept stabbing it's pointy metal spider legs into their feet...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T05:01:34-07:00","id":1110515,"title":"","content":"Finally got my hands on the latest void engineers book - excellent stuff to sink my teeth into, and helping me get my head around this topic, and inspire me too!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T08:54:07-07:00","id":1110559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eyrelliah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107226-space-tellurian-vs-technocratic-paradigm?p=1110515#post1110515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally got my hands on the latest void engineers book - excellent stuff to sink my teeth into, and helping me get my head around this topic, and inspire me too!</div> </div> </div> </div>It really explicitly does not deal with the Tellurian side of things in favor of Conventional Space, even those versions of the Tellurian that have analogous aspects. But, in so many ways, that's as it should be. The VEs have set themselves up with more then enough to do. Particularly with Threat Null out there....<br /> <br /> Not that I would mind seeing Etherspace dealt with similarly in a future Etherite splat. Or even some small sections on, say, venturing into &quot;Ptolomaic Space&quot; (ya know, all the crystal spheres and the like) in a Hermeitc book and so on. Since what one finds out there is often entirely congruent with what one is looking for for mages, it wouldn't hurt to dig into that a little (a lot?) more.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T06:47:35-07:00","id":1110823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that I would mind seeing Etherspace dealt with similarly in a future Etherite splat. Or even some small sections on, say, venturing into &quot;Ptolomaic Space&quot; (ya know, all the crystal spheres and the like) in a Hermeitc book and so on. Since what one finds out there is often entirely congruent with what one is looking for for mages, it wouldn't hurt to dig into that a little (a lot?) more.</div> </div> </div> </div>A whole book could be written just about how indians, wizards, astronauts, etc. are supposed to fight for supremacy on the heavens.<br /> We could call it: Ascension Across the Heavens. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Right now all that can be said about how ST the Umbra in Mage it's: &quot;do what thou wilt shall be whole of the law&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T07:25:53-07:00","id":1110840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107226-space-tellurian-vs-technocratic-paradigm?p=1110823#post1110823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We could call it: Ascension Across the Heavens. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>A name that would also show off the detachedness of some of the True Mages, if one considers that most humans cannot go into the conventional space, or the Etherspace, at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 07-07-2017, 05:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T09:41:13-07:00","id":1110892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107226-space-tellurian-vs-technocratic-paradigm?p=1110823#post1110823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A whole book could be written just about how indians, wizards, astronauts, etc. are supposed to fight for supremacy on the heavens.<br /> We could call it: Ascension Across the Heavens. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Right now all that can be said about how ST the Umbra in Mage it's: &quot;do what thou wilt shall be whole of the law&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It has to account for full-on Mage goofiness to the level that it undermines the tone of many games. If all the versions of &quot;space&quot; in the Umbra are coterminal, there are issues. Some games have no problem having a VE Voidship that has to obey the laws of physics as modern science understands them (spin for gravity or it's either zero-g or everyone is drifting backwards against the direction of acceleration, inertia is a big deal in space, vacuum is a thing and it's a nasty one, distances are VAST, etc.) and have a shaman on a visionquest just stroll-on by, viewing the same area as a pleasant grassland dotted with shrubbery. (So is there a spaceship hanging in mid-air over the shaman's &quot;field of grass&quot;, or does his perception of it get &quot;shaman-ized&quot; and it's like a big metal bird or a &quot;sky-whale&quot; or something similar? Likewise, do the VE's perceive the shaman as a guy &quot;walking on vacuum&quot; or do they see some weird human with all this EDE &quot;tech&quot;?) Meanwhile, a full-on Edwardian clipper ship re-rigged for etheric travel is plying it's way within view and a Hermetic in spirit form with a guide is doing a Dante-esque/Kepler's sci-fi novel transition from one crystal sphere to another....<br /> <br /> If they are not, then the various versions of &quot;space&quot; don't co-exist and are occurring on different levels of &quot;reality&quot; (whatever that means), which makes more sense but it means that no group is playing on the same &quot;field&quot; as the others and wouldn't be aware of the other folks in the vicinity without trying actively to do so and, even then, probably having difficulty interacting....<br /> <br /> Either way, there are issues. The first way, might be fun, but it's definitely going to be high on the weirdness scale. The second effectively limits Umbra groups to whatever version of the Umbra they are entering and excludes the rest. Or the Umbra is just so &quot;dreamy&quot; with everyone seeing what they want to see and fitting what they see into how they wish to understand it...<br /> <br /> And some of those ways work better for some play styles or types of Mage games than others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T11:37:12-07:00","id":1110930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107226-space-tellurian-vs-technocratic-paradigm?p=1110892#post1110892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And some of those ways work better for some play styles or types of Mage games than others.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I started this thread, I was quite excited about the umbra and how to bring it into my game; now I've gone through wanting to get away from it entirely to deciding I want to use it quite sparingly. &quot;My&quot; umbra will be pretty Traditional (with a capital T), although I'm tempted to have a lost Void Engineer stagger through a remote gate or send a desperate message that a player intercepts. Someone worthy of sympathy to challenge the loathing for the technocracy that I've instilled in the players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T06:43:22-07:00","id":1112644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107226-space-tellurian-vs-technocratic-paradigm?p=1109905#post1109905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The others were pure Etherite. Well... except for the one whose body was infected with fungus that resisted their scientific efforts to cure. He ended up as a brain in a jar and couldn't really do any science anymore. Eventually, they built a little chassis with spider legs on it for the brain to walk around on it's own. Said character was very upset with the rest of the group and kept stabbing it's pointy metal spider legs into their feet...</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds fun. Could he do science with his little chassis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13562-lordmagnusen","name":"lordmagnusen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T14:03:44-07:00","id":1112905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lordmagnusen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107226-space-tellurian-vs-technocratic-paradigm?p=1112644#post1112644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds fun. Could he do science with his little chassis?</div> </div> </div> </div>He was mostly just pissed off and pokey. He didn't want to interact with the other players and seemed headed for &quot;evil brain in a jar&quot;. The player in question was cool with that as he had to leave the game to get his highly classified job in SIGINT. So the players left the brain behind on a space station where it would be well-cared for. Soon after, they botched a &quot;short cut through hyperspace&quot; roll and ended up getting thrown several years into the future. There (then?), I ran the character as an NPC (with the blessing of his former player). He had a &quot;perfected&quot; version of his original body that had been grown for him in a vat. He was running a small armada of an upgraded warship-version the PC's ship. And was a complete and total ass to them for the rest of the chronicle. The proverbial thorn in their sides. (Though they did reconcile for the grand finale.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T17:39:07-07:00","id":1113006,"title":"","content":"One aspect to exploit in an Umbral explorers game is the clash between the consensual reality of the explorers (Void Engineers, Etherites, Hermeticists, etc) and that of planets and civilizations they encounter &quot;out there&quot;.<br /> <br /> All of those alien races and worlds that make no sense are possibilities here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T06:51:20-07:00","id":1114560,"title":"","content":"Sounds like a lot of fun, Ajax.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13562-lordmagnusen","name":"lordmagnusen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}